### Bug Found & Fixed (Test Defect, No Source Code Change)

**Test:** `I-C-02 — test_upload_init_duplicate_short_circuit`  
**Failure:** `sqlalchemy.exc.IntegrityError: UNIQUE constraint failed: uploaded_files.master_hash`  
**Root Cause:** The test incorrectly inserted a second `UploadedFile` row with the same `master_hash` as an already-seeded file. The `uploaded_files.master_hash` column has a `UNIQUE` constraint (by design — the hash is the global deduplication key). The test was redundant: since the duplicate_short_circuit path requires only an existing `DatasetFolderFilesMapping` pointing to the same file, no second file row was needed.  
**Fix:** Removed the second `UploadedFile` insert. Used a distinct unique hash for the seeded file and constructed only the mapping row. Test passes after fix.  
**Source Code:** No changes to production code. Defect was in test scaffolding only.

